  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Missouri totaled $9.7B in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 30.4% year over year. Award activity in the state shows 97,519 awards with an average award size of $99.7K. Fiscal-year obligations have fluctuated: FY21 was $13.3B, FY22 was $11.2B, FY23 was $15.6B, FY24 was $16.2B, FY25 was $14B, and FY26 is $9.7B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $6.7B obligated, followed by the Department of Energy with $2.1B. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $3B, and Facilities Support Services follows with $2.2B. THE BOEING COMPANY is the largest vendor by obligations at $4.3B, with HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC next at $2.1B. This mix shows heavy concentration in defense and energy buyers, large aerospace and support-industry awards, and a substantial share of obligations flowing to a few big vendors.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have federal obligations trended in Missouri recently?",
        "body": "Fiscal-year obligations reached $16.2B in FY24 before falling to $14B in FY25 and to $9.7B in FY26 to date. Obligations fell 30.4% year over year. Award count through FY26 to date is 97,519 with an average award size of $99.7K. The last five completed fiscal years and current year to date show volatility, with peaks in FY23 and FY24."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors account for the biggest share of spending in Missouri?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $6.7B in FY2026 to date and the Department of Energy obligated $2.1B. THE BOEING COMPANY received $4.3B and HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC received $2.1B in obligations. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest industry at $3B, and Facilities Support Services is next at $2.2B."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Missouri?",
      "a": "Missouri received $9.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Total obligations over recent years were $13.3B in FY21, $11.2B in FY22, $15.6B in FY23, $16.2B in FY24, $14B in FY25, and $9.7B in FY26 to date. Award activity in FY26 to date shows 97,519 awards with an average award size of $99.7K."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Missouri?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense awards the most contracts in Missouri, obligating $6.7B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy is the second largest buyer with $2.1B in obligations. Other notable buyers include the Department of Agriculture at $213M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $207M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Missouri?",
      "a": "THE BOEING COMPANY and HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC are the largest federal contractors in Missouri, with THE BOEING COMPANY receiving $4.3B and HONEYWELL receiving $2.1B in FY2026 to date. EVERNORTH FEDERAL SERVICES INC and a separate THE BOEING COMPANY entry follow with $687M and $673M respectively, and WORLD WIDE TECHNOLOGY LLC received $196M."
